# Hackathon speed

Frontier Cascadia, Saturday Sep 12 2026, Founders Hall, UW. Timed. Speed wins. Do not serialize work a second agent could have started.

## Model

Every Task / subagent call must set `model` to `cursor-grok-4.6-high-fast`. Do not inherit. Do not pick another slug. Do not wait for the user to name the model.

## Subagents

If the request can split, launch many Task subagents in one turn. Independent files, pages, bugs, research vs implement, server vs site. One agent per chunk. Prefer background so the parent stays free.

Do not wait for `/multitask`. Do not do a solo pass on a list that is already independent. Skip fan-out only when step B needs step A's output, both would edit the same hot file, or the change is one tiny file.

Give each subagent a full prompt: goal, paths, hackathon git rules (main only, pull then push), and what to return. They cannot see this chat.

## Context they need

Team JYPE is shipping EPSynapse at `epsynapse.com` during a live Saturday hackathon. Several people and agents commit to `main` at once. Pull before you edit. Touch only the files you need. Push `main` when a change is done. Full rules live in `AGENTS.md`.
